Z||000000||85fierose||03-15-2000||11:54 PM||||I recently installed a ram air scoop on the side of my 85 SE that had not be driven in a least 2 months. After driving it with the new scoop on there is a very pronounced stutter durring acceleration in gears 1,2,&3. Push it hard enough and it will backfire up the throttle body and out the intake. Is this due to the scoop feeding the engine to much air or do i have another problem here? Thanks for your help!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick||03-16-2000||01:41 AM||||<BR>Unless you've sucked a small pedestrian into your intake system, I'd say your problems are elsewhere.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||03-16-2000||01:45 AM||||It sounds like your distributor timing is advanced too much.<P>Pat, I'm LOL...good one!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
